	<section_number>45.2-749</section_number>
	<catch_line> Refuge from moving traffic</catch_line>
	<text>
		Upon the approach of moving traffic, any miner not engaged in haulage operations shall take refuge in a shelter hole or other place of safety.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1950, § 45-69.5; 1954, c. 191; 1966, c. 594, § 45.1-71; 1994, c. 28, § 45.1-161.138; 2021, Sp. Sess. I, c. 387.</history>
